# install --boot (typed): BOOT, a FAT32 volume tools/mkfs made, made a
# Raspberry Pi 5's boot partition from stand-ins for the Pi's /boot,
# since QEMU's initramfs has none. First from /etc/nodtb, with no device
# tree: its files copied and input.bin written, an initramfs of the
# system running, with the note that the card needs the Pi's device
# trees. Then from /etc/boot, a device tree among its files, with no
# note; --root data makes its cmdline.txt boot data, an L0FS volume of a
# fixed UUID. Then refused with no boot files, onto no volume, and with
# the boot volume as its own root.
start /bin/sh
start /sbin/uart noecho
start /sbin/virtio-blk
start /sbin/fs
dev /sbin/uart
dev /sbin/virtio-blk
